      "observed": "In the Water Level Sensor/Switches section, PR1 (LiDAR) is drawn connected to H1 and carries the global labels +5V, GND, I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA, and EZO_PDIS. Unlike the optional PR5/PR6 sensors, PR1 is not crossed out or marked DNP.",
      "expected": "The specification states that PR1 is documented but not implemented in the r2 design: its pins are free/on_board no and it is not connected to any net.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Water Level Sensor/Switches: PR1 LiDAR connected to H1 PB_1.25mm with labels I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA, EZO_PDIS (page 1)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no, in_bom: yes, and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If built as drawn, an unintended LiDAR module is connected to the main I2C bus and to the EZO_PDIS control net, changing bus loading/addresses and possibly interfering with the isolator power-disable function.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T5", "T3"],
      "pins": ["T5.1", "T5.2", "T5.3", "T3.1", "T3.2", "T3.3"],
      "nets": ["ATO_VALVE", "+24V", "GND", "+24V_FB"],
      "observed": "The ATO Valve section shows the low-side valve switch as T5 A03400A, while T3 AON6407 appears in the Power Train reverse-polarity position.",
      "expected": "The specification identifies T3 — AON6407 as the ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "ATO Valve: ATO_VALVE -> R10 -> T4 -> T5 A03400A (page 1 bottom)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "T3 — AON6407 ... ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO valve is driven by a different MOSFET than intended, with a lower voltage rating, reducing margin against inductive transients on the 24 V valve load and potentially causing premature failure.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains a clear deviation from the specification: PR1 LiDAR is wired to the main I2C/EZO_PDIS nets even though the spec says it should be unconnected. A secondary possible deviation is that the ATO valve uses T5 A03400A instead of the specified T3 AON6407."
}

